event this vulnerability start by identifying if the framework or library leveraged has built-in features or offers plugins for CSRF protection. CSRF tokens should be unique and securely random. The `Synchronizer Token` or `Double Submit Cookie` patterns with defense-in- depth mechanisms such as the `sameSite` cookie flag can help prevent CSRF. For more information, see: [Cross-site request forgery prevention](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross- Site_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"java.servlets.security.audit.cookie-missing-samesite.cookie-missing-samesite"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"b0bc9f21937f1e0d4b7f416e404d80ec385a2b148eb018145e194d12cbfe753511d9297c7b7a0d14f37c36aefc8a5ee9f7d1a4c27553b16b4ed864d6dc2113a7_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src/main/java/org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest00653.java","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":49,"endLine":55,"snippet":{"text":"        int r = new java.util.Random().nextInt();"},"startColumn":17,"startLine":55}}}],"message":{"text":"Detected use of the functions `Math.random()` or `java.util.Random()`. These are both not cryptographically strong random number generators (RNGs). If you are using these RNGs to create passwords or secret tokens, use `java.security.SecureRandom` instead."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"java.lang.security.audit.crypto.weak-random.weak-random"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"262b6930778f13a1eed179a1ef48b39c665d9c7b310f6b939898a546126f0760e05469b532d634b232c2ab814ff6ffc69bacad3bc386bb7dbf7dbc4fc687b109_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"src/main/java/org/owasp/benchmark/testcode/BenchmarkTest00653.java","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":44,"endLine":90,"snippet":{"text":"            response.addCookie(rememberMe);"},"startColumn":13,"startLine":90}}}],"message":{"text":"The application does not appear to verify inbound requests which 